---
import Photo from '../components/Photo.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { PHOTOS } from '../lib/photos';

// Photos are set in src/lib/photos.ts (PHOTOS.about, top to bottom).
const [first, second, third] = PHOTOS.about;
const photoSizes = '(min-width: 48em) 40vw, 100vw';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="About"
	description="Yoan Krastev is a former risk consultant writing essays on work, ambition and leaving stable paths."
>
	<header class="page-header">
		<h1>About</h1>
	</header>

	<!--
		TODO: replace the placeholder copy below with your own.
		Three rows alternate photo and text (photo left, right, left), then a closing paragraph spans the page.
		On phones every row stacks: photo, then text.
	-->
	<div class="rows">
		<section class="row">
			<Photo photo={first} sizes={photoSizes} />
			<div class="prose">
				<p>
					Placeholder, row one. Who you are in a few sentences, and what you write about. Something
					like: I spent the last several years as a risk consultant, advising banks on what could go
					wrong, and I’m now leaving finance to write full time.
				</p>
				<p>
					A second short paragraph can go here if you need it. Keep each row to roughly the height of
					its photo so the page stays balanced.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="row flip">
			<Photo photo={second} sizes={photoSizes} />
			<div class="prose">
				<p>
					Placeholder, row two. Why you write, and who it’s for. The reader you have in mind is
					probably someone a few years into a good corporate career, doing well by every external
					measure, and quietly asking whether this is the life they meant to build.
				</p>
				<p>
					This is a good place for the moment or the reasoning behind leaving: what you saw, what you
					weighed, what finally tipped it.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="row">
			<Photo photo={third} sizes={photoSizes} />
			<div class="prose">
				<p>
					Placeholder, row three. What you’re doing now and what’s next: the writing, the newsletter,
					the book these essays are slowly becoming.
				</p>
				<p>
					Anything that makes you more than a job title belongs here too: where you live, what you read,
					what you do when you’re not working.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>
	</div>

	<div class="closing prose">
		<p>
			Placeholder, closing paragraph. What readers can expect, and where to go next: start with the <a
				href="/articles/">articles</a
			>, or get new essays by <a href="/newsletter/">email</a>. You can also find me on LinkedIn and
			Instagram, linked below.
		</p>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.rows {
		display: grid;
		gap: 3.5rem;
	}

	.row {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1.5rem;
	}

	.row .prose {
		max-width: var(--measure);
	}

	@media (min-width: 48em) {
		.rows {
			gap: 6rem;
		}

		.row {
			grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 7fr);
			align-items: center;
			gap: 4rem;
		}

		/* Flipped rows put the photo on the right. */
		.row.flip {
			grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 7fr) minmax(0, 5fr);
		}

		.row.flip > :global(.photo) {
			order: 2;
		}

		.row.flip .prose {
			justify-self: end;
		}
	}

	.closing {
		max-width: 36em;
		margin-top: 5rem;
		font-size: var(--text-closing);
		line-height: 1.55;
	}

	@media (min-width: 48em) {
		.closing {
			margin-top: 7rem;
		}
	}
</style>
